WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.400
You would be hard-pressed to find many folks who&nbsp;
don't know Indiana Jones nowadays. The legacy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.000
of the "Indiana Jones" films is enduring,&nbsp;
thanks in part to it having no shortage of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
memorable moments. Here are some of the most&nbsp;
paused scenes in the "Indiana Jones" movies.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:16.000
In the opening sequence of "Raiders of&nbsp;
The Lost Ark," director Steven Spielberg&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.160
does an incredible job of letting us know&nbsp;
exactly what Indiana Jones is all about.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:24.720
There are puzzles, traps, betrayal, and a&nbsp;
giant boulder hell-bent on smooshing our hero.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.800
Indy navigates a sequence of deadly traps&nbsp;
and arrives at the treasure he seeks.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.520
We're then left in suspense as he stares down a&nbsp;
grimacing, gold relic. The moment hangs in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:38.480
air for longer than expected, but rather than the&nbsp;
hesitation making us anxious, we wait patiently.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:42.400
We trust that Indy knows what he’s doing. Given&nbsp;
that we only met this man minutes earlier,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:46.720
it's quite an achievement. Plus, we get to find&nbsp;
out what that sack full of sand is all about.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:51.600
Indiana Jones presents himself as a fearless&nbsp;
protagonist throughout the entire film series.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:54.800
However, there's no denying the fear&nbsp;
in his eyes when faced with a serpent.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.480
"I hate snakes Jacque! I hate 'em!"

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:02.080
"Come on, show a little backbone will ya?"

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:05.600
The temple which houses the titular Ark&nbsp;
is crawling with the slithery devils — a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:08.880
setting befitting the dangerous power&nbsp;
contained within the Ark of the Covenant.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:13.040
Indy hijacks a portion of the Nazi dig site in&nbsp;
the desert once he discovers the real location&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:17.040
of the Ark. There's a moment that follows when&nbsp;
Indy falls to the ground and looks up to discover&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:21.760
he's face-to-face with a hissing cobra. He locks&nbsp;
eyes with the creature before scrambling away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:25.840
and in that moment, you see the normally&nbsp;
stoic action hero have a face of pure panic.

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:30.960
Even if you lock him in an ancient, snake-riddled&nbsp;
throne room that hasn't been opened in thousands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:34.560
of years, Indiana Jones will still find&nbsp;
an exit — which in this instance is also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:38.720
conveniently near a Nazi-occupied air strip.&nbsp;
Good thing, too, because at this point in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:43.040
"Raiders," it's been far too long since we've&nbsp;
seen Indiana engage in fisticuffs. Fortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:47.520
our lust for action is satiated by a burly,&nbsp;
mustachioed Nazi who is eager for battle.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:50.960
Indy isn't always the top dog in a fight,&nbsp;
but what he lacks in fighting prowess,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:54.320
he makes up for in ingenuity. His&nbsp;
enemy in this scene looks formidable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:58.240
but Indy always manages to find a clever&nbsp;
way to overcome his opponent. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:03.360
in this case, defeating this gladiator Nazi on&nbsp;
the airstrip is entirely a matter of blind luck.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:07.360
The series of events that has to happen for&nbsp;
this Final Boss to go face-first into airplane&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:11.280
propeller blades borders is fantastically&nbsp;
silly and truly a wonder to behold.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:15.440
The Ark of the Covenant is shrouded&nbsp;
in mystery for most of the first film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:20.160
We're left in the dark as to what exactly is&nbsp;
contained within that beautiful, gold sarcophagus.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:24.880
After Indy combats Nazis across the globe for&nbsp;
over 90 minutes, it's time for the final reveal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:28.240
of The Ark. With all we have emotionally&nbsp;
invested in the journey, what lies inside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:32.480
that ancient tomb best be mind-blowing&nbsp;
... and it lives up to that expectation.

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:36.800
When Marion is nabbed by the evildoers, Indy&nbsp;
trails them atop a submarine, eventually arriving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:41.840
at an isolated island. Indy doesn't do so well in&nbsp;
foiling any plans and winds up tied to a stake on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:46.640
a mountain top while the bad guys ceremoniously&nbsp;
open The Ark. What's unleashed is an unholy wave&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:51.440
of destruction among the Nazis as the spirits whip&nbsp;
around and annihilate anything that looks at them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:55.457
a viewing experience that continues to&nbsp;
deliver the goods over and over again.

00:02:55.457 --> 00:03:04.368
[Lots of screaming as faces melt]

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:09.280
The opening scene of "Temple of Doom" had a lot&nbsp;
to live up to, considering the now-iconic boulder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:13.440
chase scene in the first film. The second film in&nbsp;
the series opens with a glamorous show tune with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:18.480
lots of sparkly dresses. Moments later, in steps&nbsp;
Indiana Jones: not clothed in his usual leather&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:23.280
jacket and fedora but in a fancy white tuxedo.&nbsp;
There's an exchange taking place between Jones&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:28.160
and some shady characters. We don't exactly know&nbsp;
what's being traded, but that's not the point.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:31.680
The point is Harrison Ford looks sharp,&nbsp;
and it's time for another adventure.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:35.520
In acknowledgement of a successful deal,&nbsp;
Indy lifts a glass of champagne and gulps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:39.280
it down. The bad men begin cackling with&nbsp;
laughter because our hero just drank&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:43.040
poison. The antidote is in an extremely&nbsp;
durable vial that winds up being kicked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:47.200
around the dance floor while the entire&nbsp;
dining room erupts into chaos. Watching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:51.440
Indy scramble about chasing the vial around&nbsp;
the dance floor is a fun, comical experience.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:56.480
When "Indiana Jones and the Temple of Doom"&nbsp;
was released in 1984, there was no such thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:01.280
as a PG-13 rating. Thanks to the nightmare&nbsp;
fuel that was tossed on an entire generation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:05.840
of kids who saw this PG-rated installment of&nbsp;
"Indiana Jones", the Motion Picture Association&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:10.320
of America decided to create a rating to&nbsp;
bridge the gap between PG and R ratings.

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:14.400
In "Temple of Doom," circumstances result in&nbsp;
Indiana and his companions being stranded in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:19.520
India after a plane crash. All roads force them&nbsp;
to a society housing a dark secret — mostly a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:23.760
mind-controlling shaman named Mola Ram, who&nbsp;
leads an army of acolytes with aspirations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:27.280
of world domination. Indy gets back-row&nbsp;
seats to one of their ceremonies and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:31.520
witnesses Ram use his bare hand to reach&nbsp;
into a man's chest and pull out his heart.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:35.680
He then holds the still-beating heart while the&nbsp;
man remains alive long enough to be lowered into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:41.200
a lava pit. As the man screams in agony below,&nbsp;
the heart in Ram's hand bursts into flames.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:45.520
It's a haunting image that certainly warranted&nbsp;
a re-examination of our movie rating system.

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:50.240
In "Temple of Doom," Indiana Jones&nbsp;
manages to escape his captors in a wild&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:53.680
mine cart ride that feels like Steven&nbsp;
Spielberg's audition for Disneyworld.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:58.080
The escape reaches a climactic moment when Indy&nbsp;
and pals are surrounded by the baddies on a rope&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:02.960
bridge extending over a canyon. A river teeming&nbsp;
with crocodiles lies several hundred feet below.

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:07.440
Out of safer options, he offers up a&nbsp;
knowing glance to his sidekick, Short Round,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:11.680
as he raises his sword to cut the bridge. He&nbsp;
knows everyone, including him and his allies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:16.000
will be sent tumbling to the cliffside along&nbsp;
with the collapsing bridge. It seems extreme,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:20.800
but staring death in the face and smirking is&nbsp;
just a part of daily life for Indiana Jones.

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:26.210
"Oh my God, oh my God is he nuts?"

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:30.466
"He no nuts - he's crazy!"

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:35.040
In "The Last Crusade", when Indy finally&nbsp;
tracks down his abducted father's location,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:39.440
he's betrayed by his would-be lover, Elsa. The&nbsp;
subtlety with which Ford and Connery act out the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:44.000
realization they both slept with the same woman&nbsp;
is a rewatchable moment all in of itself here.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:48.080
Father and son end up being tied up together as&nbsp;
the Nazis rummage through all their research, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:53.120
the real fun begins when Connery fumbles a Zippo&nbsp;
lighter and sends their lush prison up in flames.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:56.720
Indy and his father are tied back-to-back&nbsp;
against some chairs and are powerless to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.720 --> 00:06:01.520
escape as the entire room ignites into flames.&nbsp;
The two men hop their way over to the fireplace&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:05.760
to escape the fire. While frantically trying to&nbsp;
free himself from his restraints, Indy discovers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:10.560
that the fireplace has a trap door leading to a&nbsp;
Nazi command room. Not exactly the help they were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:15.440
hoping for because the soldiers immediately open&nbsp;
fire on them. What follows is a humorous sequence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:19.840
of events involving deception and locking&nbsp;
a bunch of Nazis in a makeshift furnace.

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:24.400
It's not easy to pick just one moment from&nbsp;
this entire motorcycle chase in "The Last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:27.760
Crusade". Everything works together&nbsp;
beautifully to create an exciting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:32.320
action-packed sequence that's also modestly&nbsp;
hilarious. Seeing the man who defined James&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:36.480
Bond in a dorky hat and glasses protecting&nbsp;
his briefcase and umbrella while refusing to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:40.240
acknowledge his son's awesomeness speaks&nbsp;
to the essence of "The Last Crusade."

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:43.360
Indiana Jones and his father escape&nbsp;
on a motorcycle with a sidecar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:47.280
but their would-be captors are in hot&nbsp;
pursuit. After rolling through a barricade,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:52.080
Indy grabs a flagpole and uses it as a lance&nbsp;
to knock an incoming Nazi off his bike.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:56.400
The loose bike zips off and crashes into&nbsp;
several other pursuers. The final motorcycle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.400 --> 00:07:00.080
baddie is finished off when Indy uses the&nbsp;
remaining fragment from his makeshift lance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:04.400
and plunges it into his enemy's wheel spokes.&nbsp;
The only acknowledgement he gets from his father&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:09.280
at this miraculous escape is an expressionless&nbsp;
face as he winds up his pocket watch. Typical.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:14.480
Those pesky Nazis always seem to find a way&nbsp;
to stay on Indy's trail and bogart any of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:18.880
discoveries. This time, they kidnap his father in&nbsp;
an attempt to force him to reveal the location of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:23.440
the Holy Grail. Good thing Henry Jones Jr. can&nbsp;
take a punch and still think straight; without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:27.680
that presence of mind, pops would be squashed&nbsp;
underneath the unforgiving tread of a tank.

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:31.360
Indy's father is being kept inside a&nbsp;
tank guarded by truckloads of soldiers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:35.200
but Indy blasts his way through them all in order&nbsp;
to help his dad get out of the musty military&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:39.840
vehicle. In a series of unfortunate events, Poppa&nbsp;
Jones falls onto the treads and is about to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:44.560
whisked off to his death before Indy pulls out his&nbsp;
trusty whip and latches it onto his father's leg.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:48.560
Indy then has to hold on to the weight of a&nbsp;
full-grown man while a Nazi jerk pummels his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:52.720
kidneys. It's an action scene that proves&nbsp;
Indiana Jones is the Alpha Archeologist.

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:58.240
All roads lead Indiana Jones, his companions,&nbsp;
and their Nazi captors to a canyon housing a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:02.880
centuries-old temple. Inside this temple is a&nbsp;
series of booby traps that can only be navigated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:08.000
with decades of research and some quick thinking.&nbsp;
Behind all these contraptions lies the Holy Grail.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:12.640
The Cup of Christ is known to be a source of&nbsp;
immortality ... but there are some caveats.

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:17.120
After water from the cup heals Henry Jones Sr.'s&nbsp;
gunshot wound, the flip-flopping Elsa picks it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:21.920
up and begins excitedly proclaiming that glory&nbsp;
is theirs. Her hubris causes her to forget the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:26.480
ancient crusader's warning to never take the&nbsp;
cup past the temple's seal. The earth rumbles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:30.960
and the ground breaks open to ultimately send&nbsp;
Elsa falling to her doom. Indy also ends up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:35.120
falling into the same crevice, but his father&nbsp;
grabs his hand at the last moment. The Holy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:39.680
Grail is barely out of reach on an opposite ledge,&nbsp;
and Indy desperately reaches out for it, despite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:44.720
his father's hand slipping. Connery injects&nbsp;
serenity into the chaos and speaks softly -

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:45.280
"Indiana…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:51.200
Let it go."

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:56.240
It's a statement that carries an extreme amount of&nbsp;
weight. It means Father Jones' life's pursuit is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:59.200
meaningless next to the life of his son.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:03.600
"Indiana Jones and the Kingdom of the Crystal&nbsp;
Skull" had almost 20 years between its release and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:08.800
1989's "The Last Crusade," and it was an absolute&nbsp;
necessity that we hit the ground running. Steven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:13.680
Spielberg made sure we got just that. The film&nbsp;
opens in a government facility we all recognize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:17.840
from the ending of the first film: a warehouse&nbsp;
containing all sorts of secrets — the Ark of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:22.080
Covenant being one of them. Indy must not be very&nbsp;
good at choosing his friends because he's betrayed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:26.240
once again by his companion and forced to&nbsp;
help the bad guys find the treasure they seek.

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:30.960
Indy winds up escaping, of course ... via a rocket&nbsp;
cart determined to shatter the land speed record.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:36.000
After that, he ends up in a small town, which he&nbsp;
slowly realizes is a dummy town — that's about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:40.160
to be on the receiving end of a nuclear&nbsp;
bomb test. Indy hops inside a lead-lined&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:43.680
refrigerator, and the blast launches&nbsp;
him far away, where he stumbles out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:49.760
unscathed. How? Because he's Indiana Jones and&nbsp;
we've still got the rest of the movie to go.

